{"id":"faculty-anurag_singh:e0013","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Dr. Anurag Singh is an Assistant Professor in the Electronics and Communication Engineering discipline. Prior to joining IIIT-NR, he has been associated as a faculty with NIT Jaipur and Thapar University, Patiala, Punjab. Dr. Anurag received his Ph.D. in Biomedical Signal Processing from Indian Institute of Technology, Guwahati and M.Tech. from Indian Institute of Information Technology, Design & Manufacturing, Jabalpur.\nDr. Singh was a part of the delegation for Indo-Japan student exchange program JENESYS-2011. He has been a recipient of International Travel Grant (Young Scientist) by Department of Science and Technology, Government of India. He has also been an invited speaker in many National level workshops. Dr. Singh has published several articles in journals and conference proceedings of international repute. He is serving as a peer reviewer in many reputed international journals and conferences. He has been an active member of IEEE, Signal Processing Society, and Engineering in Medicine and Biology Society.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
